    "problem": "Understanding the Asian monsoon's response to the recent warming hiatus is challenging because the unprecedented combination of Pacific cooling and Indian Ocean warming contradicts the expected basin-wide cooling typically associated with La Ni\u00f1a-like events, making its regional impacts unclear.",
    "method": "The authors use an atmospheric general circulation model to conduct ensemble sensitivity experiments, prescribing sea surface temperature anomalies to isolate the individual effects of recent Pacific cooling and Indian Ocean warming on Asian monsoon rainfall and circulation.",
    "task": "The task is to use atmospheric model experiments to determine the combined and individual effects of recent tropical Pacific cooling and Indian Ocean warming on Asian monsoon rainfall anomalies during the early 21st-century global warming hiatus.",
